WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:04.680
For years, Marvel fans have asked for a solo
movie centered on Black Widow.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:09.440
She's appeared as a supporting character or
popped up in a cameo in "Iron Man 2," "The

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:14.150
Avengers," "Captain America: The Winter Soldier,"
"Avengers: Age of Ultron," "Captain Marvel,"

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:18.920
"Captain America: Civil War," "Avengers: Infinity
War," and "Avengers: Endgame."

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:23.540
Up until this point, she's been the superhero
equivalent of a bridesmaid without ever being

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:24.540
a bride.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:29.340
That all changed on July 9th, when Black Widow
finally got the solo adventure she so richly

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.340
deserves.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:34.090
The movie accomplishes a great deal within
its 134-minute runtime.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:37.719
It proves Natasha can save the day even without
super-human powers.

00:00:37.719 --> 00:00:41.820
It gives her death in "Avengers: Endgame"
more meaning by showing how much her found

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:44.180
family within the Avengers meant to her.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:48.649
And it introduces a ton of fun, new characters
that have the potential to pop up in other

00:00:48.649 --> 00:00:50.059
Marvel projects.

00:00:50.059 --> 00:00:54.760
If the "Black Widow" post-credits scene is
any indication, Natasha's sister figure Yelena

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:59.809
Belova will be seen again, but we also hope
this film isn't the last time we see Alexei

00:00:59.809 --> 00:01:02.230
Shostakov, aka the Red Guardian.

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:06.660
He's effectively the Russian version of Captain
America, who believes he's on equal footing

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:11.030
with Steve Rogers, and is essentially the
walking embodiment of the Cold War.

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:14.070
Plus, he has more than a few tattoos to show
off his heritage.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:18.190
When Natasha and Yelena break Alexei out of
prison, we get a good look at the various

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:20.730
tattoos he's acquired over the years.

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.220
One of these will only make sense if you can
read Russian.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.750
On Alexei's bicep, you might notice two roses.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:28.360
Inked underneath the flowers are a couple
of Russian words.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:33.590
Translated into English, these words are actually
the names: "Natasha" and "Yelena," respectively.

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:37.530
This shows that all of these years later,
Alexei always remembered the two girls who

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.790
pretended to be his daughters while they lived
in the United States.

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:46.920
It's a vital Easter egg because Alexei, Natasha,
Yelena, and Melina Vostokoff weren't a biological

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:47.920
family.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:52.230
They were put together by villainous forces
to spy on Americans, and after they escaped

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:56.440
from Ohio, they didn't see each other again
until the events of "Black Widow."

00:01:56.440 --> 00:02:01.120
It would be easy to assume Alexei didn't form
an emotional attachment to his faux daughters,

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:04.720
but as his tattoo attests, he always carried
a part of them with him.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:09.019
If you look carefully, you may notice that
in addition to the rose tattoo for his "daughters,"

00:02:09.019 --> 00:02:11.180
he also has one of his "wife" — Melina.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:14.299
You have to look on his left-hand side next
to his neck.

00:02:14.299 --> 00:02:18.159
There's an image of a woman sporting a bob
haircut, and there's no doubt about it that

00:02:18.159 --> 00:02:20.219
he's memorialized Melina on his skin.

00:02:20.219 --> 00:02:25.230
Out of all the tattoos featured on Alexei's
body, actor David Harbour has said that Melina's

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:28.010
portrait holds a special place in his heart.

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:29.019
As he told Variety,

00:02:29.019 --> 00:02:32.700
"That was probably my favorite one because
I love Rachel Weisz."

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.090
That's likely a big reason why when they finally
reunite, they flirt with each other like old

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.459
high school sweethearts.

00:02:38.459 --> 00:02:42.590
Hopefully, the two rekindled their relationship
when they went off together at the end of

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:43.590
the movie.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:47.970
It would be awfully awkward if Alexei dated
other women on the outside and had to explain

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:50.430
why he has Rachel Weisz's face on his shoulder.

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:53.189
You might've also noticed Red Guardian has
writing on his knuckles.

00:02:53.189 --> 00:02:56.599
No, he's not a Hells Angels member with "love"
and "hate" on his hands.

00:02:56.599 --> 00:03:00.659
If you pay attention, you may realize what
he actually has written across his fingers

00:03:00.659 --> 00:03:02.079
is "Karl Marx."

00:03:02.079 --> 00:03:06.760
Marx was a philosopher best known for writing
"The Communist Manifesto," and his ideas played

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:11.250
a significant role in the formation of the
20th century Russian Revolution.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:15.980
It appears Marx's ideology is alive and well
in whatever prison Alexei was locked up in

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:16.980
for so many years.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:21.859
As a symbol of the Soviet Union, it makes
sense for Alexei to have tattoos celebrating

00:03:21.859 --> 00:03:25.040
Russia's history — and that's not even the
only one he has on his body.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:28.319
In an interview with Inverse, actor David
Harbour mentioned,

00:03:28.319 --> 00:03:31.430
"There's other stuff that's personal, stuff
that's communist.

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:34.879
He has a tattoo of Lenin on his belly, I don't
know if you see it."

00:03:34.879 --> 00:03:39.450
The Red Guardian getting Vladimir Lenin tattooed
on his body and having Karl Marx's name on

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:44.620
his hands is basically the equivalent of Captain
America getting a giant tattoo of a bald eagle

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:47.950
on his chest and having his knuckles read,
"John Jay."

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:50.790
We suppose that option's still available for
John Walker to do.

